WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.434
-Wait a minute.
-Standing ovation!

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.801
-Did Kate Beckinsale
get a standing ovation?

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:06.267
-No, no, they left. They left.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:09.367
They were waiting for you.
-They got popcorn in the lobby.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:10.701
-Kate did get
a standing ovation.

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:14.133
But you, Rainn, are special
because you got one now.

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.734
-Oh, okay. Great. Great.

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:17.267
-Rainn, it is so great
to see you.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.033
-It's good to see you.
-Congrats on the new book.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.901
-Thank you so much.
-Are you excited about this?

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:22.033
-I am s--
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.901
Thank you.

00:00:23.901 --> 00:00:25.734
Will the book
get a standing ovation?

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.534
-Yes, the book will get
a standing ovation.

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:30.167
-Yeah, I worked three
and a half years on this sucker.

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:33.567
Yeah. I'm so excited
to release it to the world.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:35.167
-I want to talk
to you about this.

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.534
But first, I wanted
to mention something

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:38.234
that I thought
made me happy.

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:41.701
Because you were
on a flight from Boston.

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.000
Do you know what
I'm talking about?

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.300
From Boston to L.A.
And here's the --

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.367
Do you want to tell the story?
-I'll tell the story.

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:50.400
So for those who didn't see,
it was a very slow news day.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.868
This was like
front-page news.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:53.834
-It was great.
It made us feel good.

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:55.901
-I was on a flight
from Boston to L.A.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:58.868
And so it was 5 1/2 hours
and sitting next to a gentleman

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:02.734
who for the entire flight
watched episodes of "The Office"

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:06.133
back to back to back to back.

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:09.000
And I was like, "What do I do?
Do I talk to him about it?

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.567
You know, how do I interact
with him about it?

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:12.868
You know,
should I even say anything?"

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:15.868
I had my COVID mask on,
so I was incognito,

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:18.501
and then I kind of nudged him.
-He had no idea?

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:20.467
-No idea the whole flight.
-The whole flight.

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:24.434
-Yeah. So I nudged him towards
the end, and then I was like,

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:26.133
"So you seem to like
that show a lot."

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.701
And he's like, "Yeah."
And I was like,

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.067
"Yeah, I heard it kind of
sucks."

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:32.434
And he's like,
"Well, you know, it kind of

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.300
starts slow in season one.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.734
You got to get used to it,
but you'll warm into it."

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:39.501
And I was slowly, slowly,

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:43.133
lowering my mask like one of
those French girls, you know?

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:44.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.901 --> 00:01:47.667
And I was like, "Oh, the first
season is kind of slow, huh?"

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:48.834
And he's like, "Yeah."
And I was like,

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:50.200
"Oh, and you have to --

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.033
It takes a little while
to warm into the characters?"

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:57.200
And then it took him like
47 seconds of talking to me.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:02.167
And then all of a sudden it was
one of those face-melting...

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:05.868
...brain explosions.
-"Oh, my God!

00:02:05.868 --> 00:02:07.834
I was sitting next to Dwight
the whole time."

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:11.234
-And we bonded
and it was beautiful.

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:13.300
-And you told him
and then you said,

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:14.601
"Can I post this?"
And he said yes.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:17.133
-Yep, yep, yep.
-And it went uber viral.

00:02:17.133 --> 00:02:18.934
-The rest is history.
-Yeah.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:21.734
Let's just take a look at this
real quick.

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:26.033
-There I am.
There's the mask.

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:28.934
I was trying to surreptitiously
do this so he wouldn't see me.

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:30.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:32.367
So I was waiting
until he was leaning forward.

00:02:32.367 --> 00:02:34.701
[ Applause ]

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:37.234
-Yeah.
-Was he eating Cap'n Crunch?

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:38.868
-Cap'n Crunch.
-He was eating Captain Crunch.

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:40.901
Yeah. Of course. Yeah.

00:02:40.901 --> 00:02:42.934
I saw you on social media.

00:02:42.934 --> 00:02:46.100
You have a lot
of interesting pets around.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:49.267
Here's one right here.
This is a -- This is --

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:51.834
-That's our peahen named Alma.
[ Audience awws ]

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:54.067
Yeah, she's a rescue peahen.

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:58.167
My wife found her at her horse
stable where we keep

00:02:58.167 --> 00:03:01.701
our pet donkey
and our pet zonkey.

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:02.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:04.834
-That's where --
-You heard it here.

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:07.400
-Yeah, you had me at donkey
and you lost me at zonkey.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.033
-Yeah.
-What is a zonkey?

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:13.567
-The spermatozoa of the zebra
enters the...

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:15.834
-Alright, alright, alright,
yeah, yeah.

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:17.801
[ Laughter ]
Hoo. Hold on.

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.601
My dad had the same talk
with me when I was a kid.

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:20.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:22.701
Yeah. He explained this.
I understand what's going on.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.467
-And we've got rescue pigs.

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:25.767
But the thing is, is like,

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:28.734
I have a long, long history
of very strange pets.

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:30.033
-You do?

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:33.734
-As a child, we lived
in Nicaragua, of all places,

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:36.100
on coastal Nicaragua
and the Caribbean coast.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.167
-Wow.
-Yeah. And we had a pet parrot

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:43.334
named Jose, and he only would
say the word Jose.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:45.767
So you try and teach him other
words, you know, you'd be like,

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:48.801
"Hello, buenos dias, hola."
He'd be like, "Jose!"

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:49.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:52.067
Morning, noon and night, Jose.

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:55.334
But the best was that
we had a pet sloth.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:56.501
[ Audience oohs ]

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:59.033
Yeah, we found
this sloth and it was hurt.

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:01.567
And we put him in a nice
little sloth cage

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:03.701
with pillows and water
and stuff like that.

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:06.234
And every night he would
break out of his cage

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:07.601
because they're nocturnal.

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:10.300
Every night he would slowly,
because they move so slow,

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.067
slowly bend the bars
of his cage.

00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:15.567
-They're strong.
-They're super strong.

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:18.167
And then every morning we'd
get up, and they're nocturnal.

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:21.767
So he's asleep when the sun
is out, and he would be gone.

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:24.167
But they are so slow.
My dad would be like,

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:25.667
"He's probably
20 or 30 feet from here."

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:26.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:28.033
-Yeah. He didn't leave
the living room yet.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.067
-Wandering around the yard

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:30.567
and literally
he'd be hanging like

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:33.234
in a shrub 20 feet away.

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:35.033
We'd go put him back
in the cage,

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:36.968
close the bars again,

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:39.133
and the same thing would happen
every single night.

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:41.367
-That sounds like
a kids book to me.

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:43.567
Yeah. The breakaway sloth.

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:45.300
I would read that
in two seconds.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.400
It's a very slow breakaway.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:49.534
I would read that.

00:04:49.534 --> 00:04:50.734
-You're always thinking of a way
to cash in.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:51.901
-Yeah, that's all I need
is the money.

00:04:51.901 --> 00:04:54.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:55.400
That's the only thing
that matters to me

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:58.000
until I read this book.
-Oh!

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.334
-No. This is fantastic,
by the way.

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.434
"Soul Boom."
-Yeah.

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:03.601
-Can we talk about what
it's about, really?

00:05:03.601 --> 00:05:06.467
-Yeah. You know, so, you know,
the first chapter is like,

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:08.067
why the hell is the guy
who played

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:10.234
Dwight writing a book
on spirituality?

00:05:10.234 --> 00:05:12.234
And I do have to admit

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:15.534
that I do kind of have
a secret inner Oprah.

00:05:15.534 --> 00:05:19.534
And I love topics
of spirituality and mysticism

00:05:19.534 --> 00:05:20.901
and religion.

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:23.334
And I think they're
really important topics.

00:05:23.334 --> 00:05:25.767
And it's a crucial time
for us to dive

00:05:25.767 --> 00:05:27.968
into some big spiritual ideas.

00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:31.033
You know, the world is hurting
and spiritual tools

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:34.400
are there for our personal
and social transformation.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.801
And it's an important
conversation.

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:37.501
-So it's not just about
religion?

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:38.868
-No, it's not really
about religion.

00:05:38.868 --> 00:05:41.734
It's more about spirituality
and spiritual tools.

00:05:41.734 --> 00:05:45.067
But I talk about, you know,
lots of big topics like life,

00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:50.767
death, the meaning of life,
the soul, suffering, sacredness,

00:05:50.767 --> 00:05:52.901
and by, you know,

00:05:52.901 --> 00:05:56.133
to try and coax some
big questions out of people.

00:05:56.133 --> 00:05:58.901
-Yeah. And it's very funny
because it's written by you.

00:05:58.901 --> 00:06:00.834
-Yes, it's funny too.
-But it makes you think

00:06:00.834 --> 00:06:02.601
and ask some tough questions

00:06:02.601 --> 00:06:05.801
and has some, like,
some nice solutions to it.

00:06:05.801 --> 00:06:08.968
One of them
I took away from this,

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:14.934
I was glancing through it.
One was that to just say that --

00:06:14.934 --> 00:06:16.267
tell someone you love them

00:06:16.267 --> 00:06:18.000
every day and that you
appreciate them.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.934
-Yes.
-Anyone.

00:06:19.934 --> 00:06:23.267
-The act of gratitude
has been scientifically proven

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:25.000
to have such
an incredible effect

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.968
on your own
personal happiness.

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:28.400
To express gratitude.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.367
So to tell someone
that you love them

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:33.100
and to tell them something
that you're grateful to them

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:36.467
for will really benefit
your own happiness,

00:06:36.467 --> 00:06:38.267
and it'll definitely
benefit theirs.

00:06:38.267 --> 00:06:39.634
It's one simple takeaway

00:06:39.634 --> 00:06:41.367
everyone can do
every single day.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:43.067
-I love that, buddy.
That's really cool.

00:06:43.067 --> 00:06:44.934
Congrats on this.
It's a big deal.

00:06:44.934 --> 00:06:46.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:46.968 --> 00:06:51.033
I also want to mention
your new series on Peacock

00:06:51.033 --> 00:06:53.868
called "Rainn Wilson
and The Geography of Bliss."

00:06:53.868 --> 00:06:56.467
It premieres
May 18th on Peacock.

00:06:56.467 --> 00:06:57.601
Tell everybody
what this is about.

00:06:57.601 --> 00:06:59.033
I'm intrigued
about this as well.

00:06:59.033 --> 00:07:00.400
-Well, we've got a lot
of celebrities

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.868
traveling the world
and sampling delicious foods.

00:07:02.868 --> 00:07:06.934
But I am traveling the world
looking for happiness.

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:07.968
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:09.367
[ Audience awws ]
Aww!

00:07:09.367 --> 00:07:10.934
-No, that's the reaction.

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:14.234
Yeah, I feel that way.
Where did you travel?

00:07:14.234 --> 00:07:16.100
-We went to Iceland.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.100
I went to Ghana
in West Africa.

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:20.601
Bulgaria.
-What'd you learn in Iceland?

00:07:20.601 --> 00:07:23.167
-Iceland.
Oh, my gosh. Iceland.

00:07:23.167 --> 00:07:26.901
You know, the Icelandic people
are among the world's happiest.

00:07:26.901 --> 00:07:28.400
And there are --

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.133
-Hygge?

00:07:30.133 --> 00:07:31.767
Hygge.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.767 --> 00:07:33.567
-Hygge?
-Hygge!

00:07:33.567 --> 00:07:36.601
-I think that's from,
like, Denmark, isn't it?

00:07:36.601 --> 00:07:38.834
-I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.834 --> 00:07:40.033
I thought it would
trigger something.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.701
I thought it would
trigger something.

00:07:41.701 --> 00:07:42.901
I thought -- I was waiting
for you to --

00:07:42.901 --> 00:07:44.901
-Say it again.
-Hygge.

00:07:44.901 --> 00:07:46.534
Yes!
That's what I'm talking about.

00:07:46.534 --> 00:07:49.367
Yes. It's like
some way of happiness.

00:07:49.367 --> 00:07:50.667
-It's a way of being.

00:07:50.667 --> 00:07:51.834
-I thought it was Icelandic,
but I might be wrong.

00:07:51.834 --> 00:07:53.300
-I think it's another
Scandinavian.

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:54.467
-Sorry.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.467 --> 00:07:56.667
-But they have such
an amazing connection.

00:07:56.667 --> 00:07:59.767
The Icelanders have
an amazing connection to nature

00:07:59.767 --> 00:08:00.968
and they love to be in nature.

00:08:00.968 --> 00:08:03.434
They love to be naked
in nature a lot,

00:08:03.434 --> 00:08:06.467
but they really -- like, no one
in Iceland believes in God,

00:08:06.467 --> 00:08:09.734
but they believe -- like 80%
of them believe in fairies.

00:08:09.734 --> 00:08:11.334
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:08:11.334 --> 00:08:12.534
-Why not?
-For real.

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:14.434
They believe in
little mysterious,

00:08:14.434 --> 00:08:18.300
mystical woodland creatures.
And they're very happy.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.734
Yeah, I learned a ton.

00:08:20.734 --> 00:08:22.234
-This show is very interesting.
I want to show a clip.

00:08:22.234 --> 00:08:24.267
Here's Rainn Wilson in Iceland

00:08:24.267 --> 00:08:26.834
for "Rainn Wilson
and the Geography of Bliss."

00:08:26.834 --> 00:08:28.033
Take a look.

00:08:28.033 --> 00:08:30.234
-Alright. Let's do this.

00:08:30.234 --> 00:08:34.834
-Good to see you guys.
-Oh!

00:08:34.834 --> 00:08:38.000
-How are you feeling?

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.601
-I don't want to be this cold.

00:08:40.601 --> 00:08:46.067
I want to drink hot chocolate,
and, um, I'm scared.

00:08:46.067 --> 00:08:47.200
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:48.601
-It's okay.
-Okay.

00:08:48.601 --> 00:08:53.734
-Your only goal now is to go
in this ocean and surrender.

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:57.701
But you tell your body
"I'm okay" because you,

00:08:57.701 --> 00:09:00.234
with your nervous system
and your head,

00:09:00.234 --> 00:09:02.267
you control everything
what your body wants to do.

00:09:02.267 --> 00:09:04.868
-[ Laughs ] Okay.
My nervous system and my hat.

00:09:04.868 --> 00:09:06.968
Okay, good. I love it.

00:09:06.968 --> 00:09:09.334
-Yeah. And she was right.

00:09:09.334 --> 00:09:10.534
-Yeah.
-And she was right.

00:09:10.534 --> 00:09:12.534
-That's right.
-Rainn Wilson, everybody.

00:09:12.534 --> 00:09:16.434
"Soul Boom" is available
tomorrow.

00:09:16.434 --> 00:09:17.868
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:09:17.868 --> 00:09:19.801
Stick around, everybody.
Congratulations.

